1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,500
This Reel died at two hundred and twelve views.

2
00:00:02,500 --> 00:00:07,000
Not because the content was bad. Because of one second. This one.

3
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:14,000
Second two. The intro animation is still playing. Nothing has moved. Nothing has been promised. The viewer’s thumb is already gone.

4
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:21,000
A retention curve doesn’t slope when this happens. It cliffs. Most of the audience gone before the content started.

5
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:28,000
The fix costs nothing. Open mid-action. Put the promise on screen inside the first second. Save the branding for the end card.

6
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:34,000
Tomorrow I’ll show you the five ways Reels die in their first three seconds. Follow so you don’t miss the autopsy.

